  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n S=(3)/(2)+(5)/(4)+(7)/(8)+...+(2n+1)/(2^n)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n S = (3)/(2) + (5)/(4) + (7)/(8) + (9)/(16) + ... + (2n+1)/(2^n)\n\nMultiply by (1)/(2):\n\n (1)/(2)S = (3)/(4) + (5)/(8) + (7)/(16) + ... + (2n-1)/(2^n) + (2n+1)/(2ⁿ⁺¹⁾\n\nSubtract the second equation from the first:\n\n S - (1)/(2)S = (3)/(2) + ((5)/(4) - (3)/(4)) + ((7)/(8) - (5)/(8)) + ((9)/(16) - (7)/(16)) + ... + ((2n+1)/(2^n) - (2n-1)/(2^n)) - (2n+1)/(2ⁿ⁺¹⁾\n\n (1)/(2)S = (3)/(2) + (2)/(4) + (2)/(8) + (2)/(16) + ... + (2)/(2^n) - (2n+1)/(2ⁿ⁺¹⁾\n\n (1)/(2)S = (3)/(2) + ((1)/(2) + (1)/(4) + (1)/(8) + ... + (1)/(2ⁿ⁻¹⁾) - (2n+1)/(2ⁿ⁺¹⁾\n\nThe terms in the parentheses form a geometric series with first term a = (1)/(2), common ratio r = (1)/(2), and n-1 terms.\n\nSum of the geometric series = frac{a(1 - rⁿ⁻¹)}{1 - r} = (frac{1)/(2)(1 - ((1)/(2))ⁿ⁻¹)}{1 - (1)/(2)} = (frac{1)/(2)(1 - (1)/(2ⁿ⁻¹⁾)}{(1)/(2)} = 1 - (1)/(2ⁿ⁻¹⁾\n\n (1)/(2)S = (3)/(2) + (1 - (1)/(2ⁿ⁻¹⁾) - (2n+1)/(2ⁿ⁺¹⁾\n\n (1)/(2)S = (3)/(2) + 1 - (2)/(2^n) - (2n+1)/(2ⁿ⁺¹⁾\n\n (1)/(2)S = (5)/(2) - (4)/(2ⁿ⁺¹⁾ - (2n+1)/(2ⁿ⁺¹⁾\n\n (1)/(2)S = (5)/(2) - (4 + 2n + 1)/(2ⁿ⁺¹⁾\n\n (1)/(2)S = (5)/(2) - (2n + 5)/(2ⁿ⁺¹⁾\n\n S = 5 - (2n + 5)/(2ⁿ⁾\n\nFor the infinite sum as n to infty, (2n + 5)/(2^n) to 0.\n\nTherefore, S = 5 - 0 = 5 (for the infinite series).\n\n**∴ The value of S is 5.**",
